WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.910
An instant hit or a swing and a miss?

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:07.310
The critics have spoken, and not all of them
are in love with "Peacemaker."

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.890
Here's what they're saying.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:14.240
Reviews for the James Gunn series "Peacemaker"
have started to trickle in ahead of its January

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:21.420
13th debut on HBO Max, and much like its titular
antihero, there's apparently a lot to like

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.279
— and abhor — about the "The Suicide Squad"
spin-off.

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:28.720
Alan Sepinwall wrote in his review for Rolling
Stone:

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:35.080
"Even in a wildly oversaturated market for
tales of hypermuscular men and women punching

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.390
their way to justice, Peacemaker stands out.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:43.030
You'll wanna taste it, even the parts that
are in incredibly bad taste."

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:48.890
He also called the show a "gloriously goofy
sendup and a sincere character study rolled

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:49.970
into one."

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:56.810
Last time viewers saw John Cena's Peacemaker
aka Chris Smith, he was walking the line between

00:00:56.810 --> 00:01:03.380
DC Comics hero and full-blown villainy after
taking the life of Joel Kinnaman's Rick Flag

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:07.030
in the final act of Gunn's "The Suicide Squad."

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:12.780
In "Peacemaker," the babbling brute is back
and on a new mission per the orders of Amanda

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.249
Waller, but there are a few things different
about him.

00:01:16.249 --> 00:01:21.020
We learn more about his backstory and get
to know the character on a more personal and

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.780
emotional level, much to some viewers' dismay.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.119
As Carly Lane wrote for Collider:

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:32.859
"Peacemaker is definitely a less bombastic
series, dealing more in relationships than

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.259
action overall.

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:39.590
But it might have also proven more successful
if it wasn't so focused on trying to render

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.350
its lead more of a likable douchebag."

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:47.090
Here's what else critics are saying so far
about the series, which as of the making of

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:52.289
this video currently holds around a 90% score
on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:01:52.289 --> 00:01:57.079
So far, the overall consensus from critics
on "Peacemaker" has been positive.

00:01:57.079 --> 00:02:03.490
But in each review, there's been one constant
critique: not enough action or edginess — most

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.640
especially, from Peacemaker.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.500
Angie Han wrote for The Hollywood Reporter:

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:13.730
"Peacemaker loses too much of the darkness
that made him compelling in the first place.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:19.420
[James Gunn] makes the character more likable,
at the cost of making him less interesting."

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.629
Collider's Carly Lane agreed, saying:

00:02:21.629 --> 00:02:26.870
"What makes Peacemaker such an interesting
and compelling character is his unrepentant

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:32.569
awfulness, and the series choosing to back-pedal
on what could be considered his defining traits

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:35.400
only makes for an aggressively fine follow-up."

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.879
When it comes to the action in "Peacemaker,"
it's obvious that Gunn didn't have as much

00:02:39.879 --> 00:02:44.220
to work with financially as he did making
"The Suicide Squad."

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.079
Fred Topel from the United Press International
wrote,

00:02:48.079 --> 00:02:53.470
"The Peacemaker series feels mostly like the
Suicide Squad comedy scenes without the big

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.660
action of a $100 million studio blockbuster.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:03.610
[...] Fight scenes are not as clear or epic
as The CW pulls off weekly in several superhero

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.610
shows.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:10.349
However, on HBO Max, the fights are punctuated
by the absurd violence that computer generated

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:11.939
visual effects allows."

00:03:11.939 --> 00:03:17.120
In spite of all this, critics ultimately believe
there's enough creative meat on the "Peacemaker"

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.790
bone to leave viewers satisfied for an entire
season.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:26.469
When it comes down to it, James Gunn's "Peacemaker"
isn't supposed to be a show that's perfect.

00:03:26.469 --> 00:03:29.209
And that's what makes it so perfect for some.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:32.370
The Daily Beast's Nick Shager said:

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:38.689
"Self-conscious but never smug, sociopathic
and yet also sweet, and timely if never preachy,

00:03:38.689 --> 00:03:44.489
it's the very sort of no-holds-barred, tongue-in-cheek
endeavor that's become Gunn's specialty."

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:48.140
Alan Sepinwall explained in Rolling Stone's
review:.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:54.069
"Between the blood and guts, the slapstick,
the political satire ... and the musical digressions

00:03:54.069 --> 00:03:56.090
... there is a lot going on here.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:02.340
Yet the series functions as a sincere character
study of its flawed hero — and the unfortunate

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:08.129
souls who have to work alongside him — just
enough for the joke to never quite wear thin."

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:12.799
As for some of the biggest highlights for
Gunn's new series, critics have propped up

00:04:12.799 --> 00:04:19.169
its character dynamics, opening credits sequences
and numerous appearances by Peacemaker's pet

00:04:19.169 --> 00:04:25.020
eagle as perfect examples of the director's
over-the-top, yet satisfying, vision.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:28.510
Speaking specifically about the intro, Sepinwall
said:

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:32.300
"It is essentially an Eighties-style music
video.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:37.169
[...] It's the kind of inspired gag that makes
a mockery of the Skip Intro option, remaining

00:04:37.169 --> 00:04:40.090
a delight every single time it comes up.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:45.280
But then, the same could be said for ol' bucket-headed
Peacemaker himself."

